Interview question
If they ask:
"What happens when an SQS message is sent to a Lambda trigger?"
Say:
"Lambda polls the SQS queue through the event source mapping. When messages are available, Lambda invokes the function with the messages as the event. 
If processing succeeds, the messages are deleted from the queue. 
If processing fails, the messages become visible again after the visibility timeout and can be retried. For repeatedly failing messages, I can configure a DLQ."
